// route-announce
//
// A tagged router and the nodes around it while it renames, announces and drops 10.30.0.0/24, which no approver covers, around an admin approval and revoke of it, under a global, an autogroup:self and a via policy. witness (odin) is the member using the router's routes, observer (thor) the other member, srv reaches the router, wit is named by no rule. witness and observer stay from hidden-peers when it ran first (RA0's note says so, and RA0 holds copies of their key and join actions) and join in RA0 otherwise. rtr's routes as the API reports them close every step. TS_DEBUG_MAP logs a stream's first keepalive only, so repeated keepalives are not in the frames.
//
// Nodes with filter rules: 3 of 5
// Steps: 12
// Captured at:    2026-10-20T12:47:45Z
// tool version:   saasprobe dd3efab44b0524074077c2aca9672118c7c4829f
